# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# project-fingerprint .gitignore
# Rule (lessons-learned §1): never let regenerable bulk into the repo.
# Track lockfiles; ignore what they regenerate. Last project: 22.8 GB
# of scaffolding around a few MB of actual research. Not again.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Lean / Mathlib ---
# Unanchored so nested project build dirs (e.g. lean/fingerprint-cores/.lake/)
# are ignored too — .lake/packages/ holds GBs of cloned deps. Not just root.
.lake/
/lake-packages/
/build/
*.olean
*.ilean
*.trace
# KEEP these (reproducible environment — do NOT ignore):
#   lean-toolchain
#   lake-manifest.json

# --- Python (search drivers: PSLQ, mpmath, sympy, OpenEvolve) ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
# KEEP: requirements.txt / pyproject.toml / uv.lock (pin the environment)

# --- Node (if any JS tooling) ---
node_modules/
# KEEP: package.json, package-lock.json

# --- Model weights & evolved-code artifacts (THE bulk for THIS project) ---
# Goedel-Prover / Leanstral checkpoints, evolution backups, search dumps.
# These will dwarf the old 22.8 GB. Never tracked. Store out-of-repo.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.ckpt
/models/
/weights/
/checkpoints/
/data/backups/
/runs/
/search_dumps/

# --- Circle-packing shakedown (regenerable bulk — vendored clone + run outputs) ---
# Track source artifacts (Dockerfile, lockfile, evaluator, example/*, witness JSON);
# ignore the cloned OpenEvolve dependency and all run output dirs.
containers/circle-packing/vendor-openevolve/
containers/circle-packing/output*/

# --- Cap-sets shakedown (Task 04): ignore run output dirs (regenerable) ---
containers/cap-sets/output*/

# --- Caches / IDE / OS ---
.cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.idea/
.vscode/        # tracked separately ONLY if a shared config is intended
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Secrets (NEVER commit) ---
.env
.env.*
*.key
*_api_key*
secrets.*
